hadiths[103]{hadithnumber,text}:
"10701","Jabir ibn Abdillah رضي الله عنهما reports that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim. He does not betray him and does not forsake him. They are one hand against others. Their blood is equal, and the least of them strives to grant protection on their behalf.""**"
"10702","Sulaym ibn Aswad reports from a man of Banu Yarbu that he came to the Prophet ﷺ and heard him addressing the people, saying: > **""The giving hand is the upper hand. Spend on your mother and your father and your sister and your brother, then the nearest then the nearest.""** A man said, O Messenger of Allah, these Banu Thalabah ibn Yarbu harmed so-and-so. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""No, no soul shall wrong another.""**"
"10703","A man of old Banu Tamim, in the time of Uthman رضي الله عنه, reported from his father that he met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, O Messenger of Allah, write for me a document that I shall not be seized for the crime of another. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""That is yours, and for every Muslim.""**"
"10704","Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said in the Farewell Pilgrimage: > **""Do not turn back after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another. No man shall be seized for the crime of his brother, nor for the crime of his father.""**"
"10705","Abdullah, meaning Ibn Masud رضي الله عنه, reports that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Do not return after me as disbelievers, some of you striking the necks of others. No man shall be seized for the crime of his father, nor for the crime of his brother.""**"
"10706","Husayn ibn Abi al-Hurr reports that his father Malik and his uncles Ubayd and Qays, sons of al-Khashkhash, came to the Prophet ﷺ and complained of a raid by a man of their cousins upon the people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote for them: > **""This is a document from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, for Malik and Ubayd. You are secure Muslims, with security for your blood and your property. You shall not be seized for the crime of another, and none shall wrong you except your own hands.""**"
"10707","Abu Ghadiyah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed them on the day of al-Aqabah and said: > **""O people, your blood and your property are sacred to you until the day you meet your Lord, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this land of yours, in this month of yours. Have I conveyed?""** They said, Yes. He said: > **""O Allah, bear witness. Do not return after me as disbelievers, some of you striking the necks of others.""**"
"10708","In one narration the reporter says, I pledged the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, with your right hand. He said: > **""Yes.""** Then he addressed them on the day of al-Aqabah with the same sermon."
"10709","Kharashah ibn al-Hurr, who was among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, reports that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Let none of you witness a slain man, lest he have been killed unjustly and wrath befall the witness.""** In another wording, a man may be killed unjustly and wrath descends upon those present and strikes the witness along with them."
"10710","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Let none of you stand in a place where a man is killed unjustly, for curse descends upon whoever is present and does not defend him. And let none of you stand in a place where a man is beaten unjustly, for curse descends upon whoever is present and does not defend him.""**"
"10711","Rifaah al-Qitbani reports that he entered upon al-Mukhtar, who offered him a cushion and claimed his brother Jibril had just risen from it. Rifaah intended to strike his neck, then remembered a hadith narrated to him by Amr ibn al-Hamiq رضي الله عنه, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whichever believer grants a believer security for his blood and then kills him, I am free of the killer.""** Ibn Majah narrates from the same Companion that such a killer shall carry a banner of treachery on the Day of Resurrection."
"10712","Amr ibn al-Hamiq رضي الله عنه reports that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever grants a man security for his blood and then kills him, I am free of the killer, even if the slain man was a disbeliever.""**"
"10713","Rifaah reports that a companion of his proposed visiting al-Mukhtar ibn Abi Ubayd, who claimed to aid the household of the Prophet ﷺ. They entered upon him at al-Khawarnaq while he sat. He showed them a sword in a sheath with rings, drew it, and a signet moved to its tip then returned to its hilt, and he placed it on his finger. The reporter thought him a sorcerer and reached for the sword hilt, but remembered the word of Sulayman ibn Mushir, from the Prophet ﷺ: > **""When a man grants you security, do not kill him.""**"
"10714","Abu Ukkashah reports that Rifaah al-Bajali entered upon al-Mukhtar ibn Abi Ubayd, and al-Mukhtar said Jibril had just left him. Rifaah remembered a hadith narrated by Rifaah ibn Surad, that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whichever man grants a man security for his blood, let him not kill him.""** Rifaah said he had already granted al-Mukhtar security for his blood, and were it not for that he would have severed his head."
"10715","Muadh رضي الله عنه reports that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever grants a man security and then kills him, Hell becomes due for him, even if the slain man was a disbeliever.""**"
"10716","Amr ibn Awf رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever claims kinship with other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah and His wrath on the Day of Resurrection. Allah shall not accept from him any obligatory or voluntary deed. Whoever kills other than his killer, upon him is the curse of Allah and His wrath on the Day of Resurrection. Allah shall not accept from him any obligatory or voluntary deed. Whoever innovates an evil or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah and His wrath on the Day of Resurrection. Allah shall not accept from him any obligatory or voluntary deed.""**"
"10717","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever fights under a banner, fighting for partisanship or aiding partisanship, his killing is that of ignorance.""**"
"10718","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever is killed in blind commotion, struck among them with a stone or a stick or a whip, his blood-money is that of mistake. Whoever is killed deliberately, it is retaliation. Whoever stands between it and justice, upon him is the curse of Allah and His wrath. Allah shall not accept from him any obligatory or voluntary deed.""**"
"10719","Amr ibn Hazm رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Deliberate killing is retaliation, and mistaken killing is blood-money.""**"
"10720","Ali رضي الله عنه and Ibn Masud رضي الله عنه said that deliberate killing is that done with a weapon."
"10721","With the same chain, Ali رضي الله عنه and Ibn Masud رضي الله عنه said that quasi-deliberate killing is with a stone and a stick."
"10722","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla reports that Ibn Masud رضي الله عنه said quasi-deliberate killing is with a stone and a stick and a whip and a shove, and in everything deliberately intended there is aggravated blood-money. Mistake is that a man throws something and it strikes wrongly."
"10723","Mahmud ibn Labid رضي الله عنه reports that on the day of Uhud the swords of the Muslims clashed over al-Yaman, the father of Hudhayfah, and killed him without recognizing him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wished to pay his blood-money, so Hudhayfah رضي الله عنه gave his blood-money as charity to the Muslims."
"10724","Ali رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him to Yemen. They came to people who had dug a pit-trap for a lion. While they crowded around it pushing one another, a man fell and clung to another, who clung to another, until four fell in. The lion wounded them, a man with a spear killed the lion, and all four died of their wounds. The kin of the first rose against the kin of the next with weapons. Ali عليه السلام came upon them and said: > **""Do you wish to fight while the Messenger of Allah is alive. I shall judge between you. If you accept, it is the judgment, otherwise restrain one another until you come to the Messenger of Allah and he judges between you. Whoever transgresses after that has no right. Gather for me from the tribes that dug the well a quarter, a third, a half, and a full blood-money. For the first a quarter, for the second a third, for the third a half.""** They refused to accept. They came to the Prophet ﷺ as he stood by the Station of Ibrahim and told him the story. He said: > **""I shall judge between you.""** He sat gathered in his cloak. A man said Ali had already judged among them. They told him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ confirmed the judgment of Ali."
"10725","In one narration, the fourth shall have the full blood-money."
"10726","Hanash ibn al-Mutamir reports that they dug a well in Yemen and a lion fell in. In the morning they looked at it. A man fell toward the well and clung to a man, who clung to another, who clung to another, until they were four, and all fell in together. The lion wounded them, and a man struck it with his spear and killed it. The people said to the first, you killed our companions and owe their blood-money. The parties nearly fought. Ali رضي الله عنه arrived and said: > **""I shall judge between you. Whoever of you accepts, his acceptance stands, and whoever is displeased has no right until you come to the Messenger of Allah and he judges between you.""** They said, Yes. He said, gather from those who dug the well a quarter blood-money, a third, a half, and a full blood-money. For the first a quarter since three perished above him, for the second a third since two perished above him, for the third a half since one perished above him, and for the last the full blood-money. He said: > **""If you accept, this is the judgment between you. If you do not accept, you have no right until you come to the Messenger of Allah.""** They came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the next year and told him. He said: > **""I shall judge between you, if Allah wills.""** He sat at the Station of Ibrahim. A man stood and said Ali had judged between them. He said: > **""How did he judge between you.""** They told him, and he said: > **""It is as he judged between you.""**"
"10727","Mirdas ibn Urwah reports that a man shot his brother and killed him, then fled. They found him with Abu Bakr رضي الله عنه and brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who granted them retaliation against him."
"10728","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ forbade retaliation upon a slave against two men."
"10729","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that a slavegirl came to Umar ibn al-Khattab رضي الله عنه and said her master accused her and seated her upon fire until her private part burned. Umar asked whether he saw it upon her or she confessed to him, and she said no to both. Umar summoned him and said, do you punish with the punishment of Allah. The man said he suspected her of misconduct without sight or confession. Umar said, by Him in whose hand is my soul, were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""No slave shall be retaliated against his master, nor a child against his father.""** I would have granted her retaliation against you. Then he brought him forth and struck him one hundred lashes, and said to her, go, you are free for the sake of Allah, a freedwoman of Allah and His Messenger. He said, I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever is burned with fire or mutilated is free, and he is the freedman of Allah and His Messenger.""**"
"10730","Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As رضي الله عنهما reports that Zinba Abu Rawh found his slavegirl with his male slave, so he cut off his nose and mutilated him. The slave came to the Prophet ﷺ, who asked: > **""Who did this to you.""** He said Zinba. The Prophet ﷺ summoned him and said: > **""What carried you to this.""** He mentioned the conduct of the slave. The Prophet ﷺ said to the slave: > **""Go, for you are free.""** The slave asked, O Messenger of Allah, whose freedman am I. He said: > **""A freedman of Allah and His Messenger.""** The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commended him to the Muslims. After the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ he came to Abu Bakr رضي الله عنه invoking the bequest of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Abu Bakr granted maintenance for him and his dependents until Abu Bakr died. Then under Umar رضي الله عنه he asked the same, and Umar asked where he wished to go. He said Egypt, so Umar wrote to the governor of Egypt to grant him land to live from."
"10731","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urged jihad one day and the people crowded over him until they pressed him. In the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was a palm-stalk stripped of thorns except one overlooked thorn. He said: > **""Move back from me like this, for you have pressed me.""** The stalk struck a man's belly and drew blood. The man went out saying, this is the deed of your Prophet, so how should others behave. Umar رضي الله عنه heard him and said, go to the Prophet ﷺ. If he struck you he will give you your right, and if you lied I shall humiliate you. The man refused to go, but Umar brought him to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and said he claims you struck him and drew blood from his belly. The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Is it true that I struck you.""** The man said, yes, O Prophet of Allah. He said: > **""Did anyone see that.""** Muslims said, O Messenger of Allah, you drew his blood without intending it. The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Take wealth for what I caused you and go.""** He said no. He said: > **""Then grant it to me.""** He said he would not. He said: > **""Then what do you want.""** He said, I wish to retaliate against you, O Prophet of Allah. The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Yes.""** The man said, come out from among them. He came out and gave the man the stalk to retaliate. The man uncovered his belly, then kissed it and said, I forgive, hoping for intercession thereby. The Prophet ﷺ praised him and gave him compensation."
"10732","Abdullah ibn Jubayr al-Khuzai رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ poked a man in the belly with a rod or a siwak. The man said, you hurt me, grant me retaliation. He gave him the stick and said: > **""Take retaliation.""** The man kissed his belly and said, rather I forgive, that you may intercede for me thereby on the Day of Resurrection."
"10733","Tariq ibn Shihab reports that the cousin of Khalid ibn al-Walid slapped a man of theirs. His uncle disputed with him to Khalid and said, O company of Quraysh, Allah did not give your faces merit over ours except by what Allah favored His Prophet ﷺ with. Khalid ibn al-Walid رضي الله عنه said, retaliate. The man told his nephew, slap back. When he raised his hand, the uncle said, leave it for Allah Almighty."
"10734","Abu Said رضي الله عنه reports that a slain man, or a dead man, was found between two villages. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded measuring between the two villages to see which was nearer. He was found nearer to one by a span, and the reporter said it is as if he still looks at the span of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He assigned liability upon the nearer one."
"10735","Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf رضي الله عنه reports that qasamah in blood occurred on the day of Khaybar. A man of the Ansar among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ was missing by night. The Ansar came and said their companion lay weltering in his blood. He said: > **""Do you know his killer.""** They said no, except that the Jews killed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Choose fifty men of them to swear by Allah their strongest oaths, then take the blood-money from them.""** They did so."
"10736","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that qasamah in ignorance was a restraint between people. Whoever swore a binding oath falsely and sinned therein was shown a punishment from Allah deterring boldness toward sacred things, so they feared binding oaths. When Allah sent Muhammad ﷺ with qasamah, the Muslims feared it more for what they had learned. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged with qasamah between two clans of the Ansar called Banu Harithah, for the Jews had killed Muhayyisah and the Jews denied it. The Prophet ﷺ called the Jews to qasamah since they claimed the blood, and commanded them that fifty leading men swear fifty oaths as to who killed him. The Jews refused the oaths. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Banu Harithah and commanded them that fifty men swear fifty oaths that the Jews killed him treacherously, thereby establishing their claim against the accused. Banu Harithah also refused the oaths. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw that, he imposed his blood-money upon the Jews, since he was found among them and in their dwellings."
"10737","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that qasamah was from the affair of ignorance, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ confirmed it to restrain people from bloodshed."
"10738","Abdullah ibn Wafid reports that the oath in blood existed in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."
"10739","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that a Jewish woman gifted the Prophet ﷺ a roasted sheep. He ate from it, then said: > **""This sheep has told me that it is poisoned.""** Bishr ibn al-Bara died from it. He sent to her: > **""What carried you to what you did.""** She said she wished to know: if you were a prophet it would not harm you, and if you were a king she would relieve people of you. He commanded concerning her and she was killed."
"10740","Abdullah, meaning Ibn Masud رضي الله عنه, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There is no retaliation except with the sword.""**"
"10741","Al-Numan ibn Bashir رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Retaliation is with the sword, and for everything else there is mistake.""** Ibn Majah narrates only his saying that there is no retaliation except with the sword."
"10742","Alqamah reports that Ibn Masud رضي الله عنه said the most restrained of people in killing are the people of faith."
"10743","Ibn Masud رضي الله عنه said concerning a man retaliated against who then dies, that his blood-money is taken by retaliation, then the blood-money of his wound is deducted from it."
"10744","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""A dirham I give toward blood-money is dearer to me than a hundred spent elsewhere.""**"
"10745","Abu Bakrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever brings something out beyond its limit and thereby strikes a man, he is liable.""**"
"10746","Imran ibn Husayn رضي الله عنه reports that a man of Hudhayl killed a man of Khuzaah in ignorance, and the Hudhali remained hidden. On the day of the Conquest, when the proclamation appeared, the Hudhali appeared. A man of Khuzaah met him and slaughtered him as a sheep is slaughtered. The matter was raised to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: > **""Did you kill him before the proclamation or after the proclamation.""** He said after the proclamation. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Had I been one to kill a believer for a disbeliever I would have killed him. Bring forth his blood-money.""** They brought forth his blood-money, and it was the first blood-money in Islam."
"10747","Maqil ibn Yasar رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The Muslims are one hand against others. Their blood is equal. No believer shall be killed for a disbeliever, nor one under covenant while in his covenant.""**"
"10748","Aishah رضي الله عنها said she found in the hilt of the sword of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ two writings: > **""The most insolent of people are one who strikes other than his striker, and a man who kills other than his killer, and a man who claims kinship with other than his benefactors. Whoever does that has disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger. Allah shall not accept from him any obligatory or voluntary deed.""** And concerning recompense: > **""The believers, their blood and their property are equal, and the least of them strives to grant protection on their behalf. No Muslim shall be killed for a disbeliever, nor one under covenant while in his covenant. People of two religions do not inherit from one another. A woman shall not be married together with her paternal aunt nor with her maternal aunt. There is no prayer after Asr until the sun sets, and a woman shall not travel three nights with other than a close male relative.""**"
"10749","Aban ibn Said ibn al-As رضي الله عنه addressed and said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ annulled every blood-claim of ignorance."
"10750","Amr ibn Awf al-Muzani رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""No exposed slain man shall be left in Islam until he is joined to a tribe.""** Ibn al-Athir says in al-Nihayah that it means a slain man found in empty land far from a village; his blood-money is paid from the public treasury and his blood is not void."
"10751","A man reports that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""There shall be a people under covenant. Whoever kills a man of them shall not smell the scent of Paradise, though its scent is found from a journey of ninety years.""**"
"10752","Abu Bakrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever kills a covenanted soul shall not smell the scent of Paradise, though its scent is found from a journey of five hundred years.""**"
"10753","In one narration: > **""A hundred years.""**"
"10754","Jundab رضي الله عنه reports that it reached him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever betrays my protection, I shall be his adversary, and whomever I oppose, I shall overcome.""**"
"10755","Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There is no contagion, no Safar omen, no Hamah, nor two completed months, and whoever breaches a covenant shall not smell the scent of Paradise.""**"
"10756","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever kills a covenanted soul without its right shall not smell the scent of Paradise, though the scent of Paradise is found from a journey of a hundred years.""** Al-Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah narrate it with seventy years."
"10757","Abdullah ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that people raided the camels of the Prophet ﷺ and drove them off, apostatized from Islam, and killed the believing shepherd of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ sent after them. They were seized, and their hands and feet were cut off and their eyes were branded."
"10758","Salamah ibn al-Akwa رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ had a servant called Yasar. He saw him pray well, freed him, and sent him among his milch-camels at al-Harrah. People of Uraynah from Yemen professed Islam outwardly and came sick with fever and swollen bellies. The Prophet ﷺ sent them to Yasar. They drank camel milk until their bellies healed. Then they attacked Yasar and slaughtered him, placed thorns in his eyes, and drove off the camels. The Prophet ﷺ sent horsemen of the Muslims after them under Kurz ibn Jabir al-Fihri. He overtook them and brought them. Their hands and feet were cut off and their eyes were branded."
"10759","Jarir رضي الله عنه reports that people of Uraynah raided the milch-camels of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ commanded that their hands and feet be cut off and their eyes be branded."
"10760","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a man bit the hand of a man, who pulled away his tooth. The Prophet ﷺ voided it."
"10761","Ismah رضي الله عنه reports that a man whose eye had been gouged came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: > **""Who struck you.""** He said, the one-eyed man of Banu so-and-so. He summoned him and said: > **""Did you gouge the eye of this man.""** He said yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged blood-money against him and said: > **""We shall not gouge his eye and leave him sightless.""**"
"10762","Abu Dharr رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whichever man lifts a veil and inserts his gaze before permission is given has committed a punishable encroachment he was not permitted. Had a man gouged his eye, it would be void. Had a man passed a door with no veil and seen the private affairs of its people, there is no sin upon him. The sin is only upon the household.""**"
"10763","Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever peeps through a curtain at a people and his eye is gouged, it is void.""**"
"10764","Abdullah ibn Amr رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged concerning a man who stabbed a man with a horn in his leg. The wounded man said, O Messenger of Allah, grant me retaliation. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: > **""Do not hasten until your wound heals.""** The man refused anything but immediate retaliation. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted him retaliation. The retaliator became lame and the retaliated one healed. The retaliator came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, O Messenger of Allah, I am lame and my fellow is healed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: > **""Did I not command you not to seek retaliation until your wound heals, and you disobeyed me. May Allah keep you far, and your wound is void.""** Then after that, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that whoever bore a wound shall not seek retaliation until healed from his wound, and when healed he may retaliate."
"10765","Jabir رضي الله عنه reports that a case was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of a man who stabbed a man in the thigh with a horn. The wounded man said, grant me retaliation, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Treat it and wait with it until you see what it becomes.""** He repeated the demand twice more with the same reply. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted him retaliation. The leg of the retaliator withered and the retaliated one healed, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ voided its blood-money."
"10766","In one narration he said: > **""Treat it and delay him a year.""**"
"10767","In one narration, a man was wounded and the Prophet ﷺ forbade retaliation against the wounder until the wounded heals."
"10768","Hudhayfah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left them while they hastened, and none of them examined a penetrating or bone-displacing wound except Amr ibn Umayr."
"10769","Umar رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""For the nose when its amputation is complete, the full blood-money. For the eye fifty, for the hand fifty, for the leg fifty, for a penetrating wound a third of a life, for a bone-displacing wound fifteen, for a bone-exposing wound five, for a tooth five, and for every finger thereof ten and ten.""**"
"10770","Ubadah ibn al-Samit رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged in the aggravated major blood-money thirty hiqqah, thirty jadhaah, twenty daughters of labun, and twenty male sons of labun."
"10771","Ubadah رضي الله عنه reports that he, meaning the Prophet ﷺ, judged in the major aggravated blood-money thirty daughters of labun, thirty hiqqah, and forty pregnant camels. And in the minor blood-money thirty daughters of labun, thirty hiqqah, twenty daughters of makhad, and twenty male sons of makhad. After the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ camels rose in price and silver fell, so Umar رضي الله عنه valued camel blood-money at six thousand dirhams, an ounce for each camel. Then camels rose and silver fell, so Umar added two thousand, two ounces for each camel. Then camels rose and dirhams fell, so Umar completed it at twelve thousand, three ounces for each camel. A third of blood-money is added in the sacred month, and another third in the sacred land. Thus the blood-money of the two sanctuaries reached twenty thousand. It was said that from desert folk their livestock is taken without burdening them with silver or gold, and from every people justice is taken in their wealth."
"10772","Al-Saib ibn Yazid رضي الله عنه reports that blood-money in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was one hundred camels of four ages: twenty-five hiqqah, twenty-five jadhaah, twenty-five daughters of makhad, and twenty-five daughters of labun. In the time of Umar, when the garrison towns were founded, Umar said not all people own camels. Camels were valued an ounce each, four thousand dirhams. Then camels rose, so Umar said value them an ounce and a half, six thousand dirhams. Then camels rose, so Umar said value them, and they were valued three ounces, twelve thousand. He imposed upon silver folk twelve thousand, upon camel folk one hundred camels, upon gold folk one thousand dinars, upon cloth folk two hundred garments each worth five dinars, upon sheep folk one thousand sheep, upon goat folk two thousand goats, and upon cattle folk two hundred cows."
"10773","Al-Shifa Umm Sulayman رضي الله عنها reports that the Prophet ﷺ employed Abu Jahm ibn Hudhayfah over spoils. He struck a man with his bow and made a bone-displacing wound. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged therein fifteen portions."
"10774","Zayd ibn Thabit رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged only three wound cases: for the skull-penetrating wound thirty-three, for the bone-displacing wound fifteen, and for the bone-exposing wound five. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged in the eye of a beast a fourth of its price."
"10775","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged in fingers ten and ten, and in the hand fifty portions. In al-Sahih only the saying that fingers are equal is narrated."
"10776","Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, stated concerning diyah, blood-money for injury: both eyes are equal, all fingers are equal, all teeth are equal, both hands are equal, and both feet are equal. That is, each member of a pair carries the same valuation, with the full diyah distributed equally over the pair. > **""Both eyes are equal, fingers are equal, teeth are equal, both hands are equal, and both feet are equal.""**"
"10777","Alqamah ibn Qays reported that Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, said: for every paired organ of the body, the full diyah lies in the two together, and for every single unpaired organ, the full diyah lies in it alone. This establishes the principle of diyah for zawjayn, paired limbs, and for wahid, solitary organs. > **""For every pair, in the two is the blood-money, and for every single organ, in it is the blood-money.""**"
"10778","Asim ibn Kulayb reported from his father that he met Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, at the seasonal gathering at Mina. He called out from behind the tent that he was so-and-so al-Jurmi and that a nephew of theirs was held captive among such-and-such tribe, and that they had offered them the faridah, obligatory compensation, of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Umar lifted the side of the tent and asked if he knew his man, and when he confirmed it, ordered that they proceed with him so that the qadiyyah, judicial decision, of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, be carried out. The narrator added that they used to relate that the decreed compensation was four camels. > **""Do you know your man? Take him with you both so that the decision of the Messenger of Allah is carried out.""**"
"10779","Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, said concerning shibh al-amd, quasi-intentional homicide: twenty-five hiqqah, camels in their fourth year, twenty-five jadhaah, camels in their fifth year, twenty-five bint makhad, young she-camels, and twenty-five bint labun, she-camels in their third year. This makes one hundred camels in graded ages. > **""Quasi-intentional killing requires twenty-five hiqqah, twenty-five jadhaah, twenty-five bint makhad, and twenty-five bint labun.""**"
"10780","Ibrahim al-Nakhai reported that Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, said concerning al-khata, accidental killing: twenty hiqqah, twenty jadhaah, twenty bint makhad, twenty ibn makhad, young male camels, and twenty bint labun. This totals one hundred camels divided into five equal age-groups. > **""For accidental killing: twenty hiqqah, twenty jadhaah, twenty bint makhad, twenty ibn makhad, and twenty bint labun.""**"
"10781","Mujahid reported that Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, said concerning the man and the woman: they are equal up to five camels. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: the woman is half of the man in everything. The first view holds equivalence in minor injuries up to a threshold, the second holds halving throughout. > **""The man and the woman are equal up to five camels. The woman is half in everything.""**"
"10782","Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said that the diyah of the dhimmi, protected non-Muslim resident, is the diyah of the Muslim. > **""The blood-money of the dhimmi is the blood-money of the Muslim.""**"
"10783","Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said that the diyah of the muahid, covenanted non-Muslim, is half the diyah of the Muslim. > **""The blood-money of the covenanted person is half the blood-money of the Muslim.""**"
"10784","Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, said that the diyah of the muahid is like the diyah of the Muslim, and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said the same. This is the reported ijtihad of two Companions equating the two in protection of blood. > **""The blood-money of the covenanted person is like the blood-money of the Muslim.""**"
"10785","Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, decreed concerning diyah al-janin, blood-money for the fetus when still in its mother's womb, that it be a ghurrah, a fine of a male slave or female slave. He gave this judgment in the case of the wife of Hamal ibn Malik ibn al-Nabighah al-Hudhali. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, also said that there is no shighar, exchange-marriage without dower, in Islam. > **""There is no shighar in Islam.""**"
"10786","Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, was present at the judgment of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in this matter. Hamal ibn Malik ibn al-Nabighah came and said he had been married to two women, one struck the other with a mistah, flat stick, killing her and her unborn child. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, decreed for her fetus a ghurrah of a slave, and that the killer be subject to retaliation. The report is transmitted through Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from Umar. > **""I was between two wives, and one struck the other with a stick, killing her and her fetus.""**"
"10787","Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that two women of Hudhayl, one killed the other, and the slain woman was pregnant. The aqilah, paternal kin liable for blood-money, of the slain woman reported that she was pregnant and had cast a dead fetus. The aqilah of the killer feared liability and protested that the fetus had neither drunk nor eaten nor cried out nor raised its voice at birth. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rebuked their rhymed pleading and decreed for the fetus a ghurrah of a male slave or female slave. > **""Is this the rhymed prose of the Jahiliyyah?""**"
"10788","Abu al-Malih al-Hudhali reported from his father that among them was Hamal ibn Malik ibn al-Nabighah, who had two wives, one Hudhali and one Amiri. The Hudhali wife struck the belly of the Amiri wife with a tent-pole, causing her to miscarry a dead fetus. The striker was brought to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with her brother Imran ibn Uwaymir. When the story was told, he ordered payment of its diyah. Imran objected that they should pay for one who neither ate nor drank nor cried out, arguing such blood is void. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, dismissed Bedouin rajaz verse, and fixed a ghurrah of a slave or slave-girl, or five hundred camels, or a horse, or one hundred twenty sheep. When the man argued her two sons, chiefs of the clan, should bear the aql, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ruled the brother is more entitled to bear it for his sister than her sons, and since the man had nothing, told Hamal, then in charge of Hudhayl charities and husband of the woman and father of the slain fetus, to take one hundred twenty sheep from Hudhayl charities under his hand, which he did. > **""Keep away from me the rajaz of the Bedouins. For it there is a ghurrah of a slave or slave-girl, or five hundred, or a horse, or one hundred twenty sheep.""**"
"10789","Abu al-Malih reported from his father, a Companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that two women quarreled and one struck the other with a staff, killing her and what was in her womb. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, decreed for the woman the aql, full blood-money, and for the fetus a ghurrah of a slave or slave-girl, or a horse, or two camels, or a stated number of sheep. A man of the killer's kin objected how they should pay for one who neither ate nor drank nor cried out, claiming such blood is void. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rebuked him, and decreed the woman's inheritance for her husband and child and the aql upon the asabah, male kin, of the killer. > **""Are you speaking in rhymed prose?""**"
"10790","Uwaymir reported that his sister Mulaykah and a woman of their clan, Umm Afif bint Masruh, were both under Hamal ibn al-Nabighah in marriage. Umm Afif, who was not pregnant, struck the pregnant Mulaykah with the mistah of her house, killing her and her fetus. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, decreed diyah for her and a ghurrah of a slave or young slave for her fetus. Her brother Ala ibn Masruh objected whether one should pay for one who neither ate nor drank nor spoke nor cried at birth, claiming such blood is void. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked if this was rhyming like the rhyming of the Jahiliyyah. > **""Is it rhyming like the rhyming of the Jahiliyyah?""**"
"10791","Abu al-Zubayr heard Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with them both, say that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, imposed the uqul, shares of blood-money, upon every batn, clan subdivision, then decreed that it is not lawful for the mawla, freedman, of a Muslim to take another as patron without his permission. This joins aqilah responsibility with preservation of wala, clientage. > **""It is not lawful for the freedman of a Muslim man to take another as patron without his permission.""**"
"10792","Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say that all sons of a woman trace their asabah, agnatic kinship, to their father, except the sons of Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, for he himself is their asabah and their father. > **""All sons of a woman, their asabah is through their father, except the sons of Fatimah, for I am their asabah and I am their father.""**"
"10793","Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said not to impose anything upon the aqilah, kin liable for blood-money, merely on the word of one who confesses. > **""Do not place upon the aqilah anything on the basis of the statement of one who confesses.""**"
"10794","Aidh ibn Said reported that Samir ibn Zuhayr al-Jisri said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that his brother Salamah ibn Zuhayr had set out migrating to Allah and His Messenger, but camel-herdsmen of Banu Ghifar met and killed him in the sacred month, with an old Jahili blood-feud between them. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, summoned them and questioned them. They said they found him driving his camels, sought to seize him, he resisted, and they killed him. The narrator did not recall whether he put them under oath or accepted their word, but he asked about the brother's Islam and found no proof, so he paid for him fifty camels for the hurmah, sanctity, of the month. The remainder of the camels in his house proved the finest and most blessed of livestock. > **""O Messenger of Allah, my brother Salamah set out migrating to Allah and His Messenger, but herdsmen of Banu Ghifar killed him in the sacred month.""**"
"10795","Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said that three deeds, whoever brings them with faith enters Paradise by whichever gate he wishes and is married to as many of the hur al-in, wide-eyed maidens, as he wishes: paying a hidden debt, pardoning his killer, and reading Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad ten times after every prescribed prayer. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, asked if even one of them suffices, and he replied that even one suffices. > **""Three deeds: whoever brings them with faith enters through whichever gate of Paradise he wishes. Or even one of them.""**"
"10796","Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said that whoever possesses one quality, Allah will marry him to the hur al-in: one who holds a hidden desirable trust and renders it from fear of Allah, or a man who pardons his killer, or a man who reads Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad after every prayer. > **""Whoever has one of them, Allah will marry him to the hur al-in.""**"
"10797","Ibn al-Samit, meaning Ubadah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said that whoever gives charity of his body, meaning forgoes retaliation for injury, Allah expiates for him sins to that measure. In another wording, whoever gives charity of anything of his body is granted reward to the measure of his charity. > **""Whoever gives charity of his body for an injury, Allah expiates for him to the measure of his sins.""**"
"10798","Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, said he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say that no man is wounded in his person and then gives it as charity, meaning forgives it, except that Allah, Blessed and Exalted, expiates for him the like of what he gave. > **""There is no man wounded in his person who then forgives it except that Allah expiates for him the like of what he forgave.""**"
"10799","A man among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, reported that he said whoever is afflicted in his body with any injury and leaves it for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, it becomes an expiation for him. > **""Whoever is afflicted in his body with anything and leaves it for Allah, it is an expiation for him.""**"
"10800","Adi ibn Thabit reported that in the time of Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him, a man smashed the mouth of another man. He was offered his diyah but refused to accept until he was given threefold. A man present said he had heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say that whoever gives charity of blood or less than it, meaning forgoes it, it becomes expiation for him from the day he was born until the day he forgave. > **""Whoever gives charity of blood or less than it, it is an expiation for him from the day he was born until the day he gave charity.""**"
"10801","Yazid ibn Mabad reported that his brother Qays ibn Mabad and Jariyah ibn Zafar quarreled over a shared pasture. Jariyah struck him and Qays struck him, severing his hand. They disputed to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Yazid said they went until they came to him and told the story. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, told the injured man to gift him his hand so that it would come to him white and sound on the Day of Resurrection, but he refused. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, told them to leave him, then said to Yazid to gift him its aql, compensation. Yazid said it is yours, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called him, gave him the diyah, said may Allah bless you, and told Jariyah ibn Zafar to take it. Yazid took it, and they recognized blessing in themselves through the supplication of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. > **""Gift me his hand, and it will come to you on the Day of Resurrection white and sound.""**"
"10802","Qatadah reported that a man who had killed another was brought before Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him. The heirs of the slain came, and one of them had pardoned. Umar asked Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, beside him what he held. Ibn Masud said he held that the killer was now protected from execution. Umar struck his shoulder and said he was a vessel filled with knowledge. > **""I hold that he is now protected from execution.""**"
"10803","Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said that the saibah, stray beast causing injury, is jubar, void of liability, the well is jubar, the mine is jubar, and in rikaz, buried treasure, is the fifth. In one transmission the word is saimah, pasturing livestock, in place of saibah. > **""The stray animal is void of liability, the well is void of liability, the mine is void of liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth.""**"
